participant "gRPC/Netty callback" as Netty
participant "EdgeGrpcSession" as Session
participant "App/Tenant Actor dispatcher" as Actor
participant "edge-service single thread" as ServiceThread
participant "edge-event-check-scheduler" as Check
participant "edge-send-scheduler" as Send
participant "GrpcCallbackExecutor" as Callback
database "DAO executor / JDBC" as DAO

Netty -> Session: onNext(RequestMsg)
Session -> DAO: connect lookup / processor calls
DAO --> Callback: ListenableFuture completion
Callback -> Session: uplink response / sync continuation

Actor -> ServiceThread: executorService.execute(EdgeSessionMsg)
ServiceThread -> ServiceThread: mutate session flags / start sync
ServiceThread -> Check: schedule event check
Check -> Session: processEdgeEvents()
Session -> DAO: read event page / attributes
DAO --> Callback: future callbacks
Callback -> Session: convert / update cursor / continue
Session -> Send: submit or schedule downlink pack
Send -> Session: sendDownlinkMsg(ResponseMsg)
Session -> Netty: outputStream.onNext()

note over Netty,DAO
Do not block Netty callbacks or Actor dispatchers.
Callback, scheduler and JDBC pools are different capacity domains.
end note
@enduml
